  "question": {
    "text": "A polarizer - analyser set is adjusted such that the intensity of light coming out of the analyser is just <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mi>%</mi></math> of the original intensity. Assuming that the polarizer - analyser set does not absorb any light, the angle by which the analyser needs to be rotated further, to reduce the output intensity to zero, is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>37</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
